        "original_id": "d3c7768d-a856-557d-b15d-7012c1a6411c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Age of Chance, Vector\n- Albums: One Thousand Years of Trouble\n- Places: Leeds, England; Sacramento, California\n- Companies: Virgin Records\n\nFacts:\n- Vector was a rock band formed in Sacramento, California, in the early 1980s by Jimmy Abegg, Steve Griffith, and Charlie Peacock.\n- Age of Chance were a British alternative rock-dance crossover band from Leeds, England, active from 1985 to 1991.\n- One Thousand Years of Trouble is the debut full-length album and second album overall by the English electronic rock band Age of Chance.\n- Virgin Records released One Thousand Years of Trouble in 1987.",
